17592186300960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301566 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301566 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301566 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301566 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301566 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6d2d80b8-7823-5a2c-a4eb-3fe09645cb4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302009 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f52d6758-b968-51b9-a5a2-6e03ab7af674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302265 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302265 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302265 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302265 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the general solution to the matrix differential equation $\\,{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1.7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1.7\\end{aligned}]x(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302265 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5878b428-f5a6-5ebd-8385-5b72ac276f64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302265 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\lambda \\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the matrix of our differential equation is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1.7t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1.7t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345514 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t} \\\\ (1-t){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345514 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345514 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "130d3616-3670-5a5c-b8da-00c9c23fef02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345547 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345547 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345547 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "163b9c8a-95d6-5825-8c03-376d7d06d2ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345621 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345621 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345621 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e9a8c81-a091-545d-84fc-e0dd993ec18b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345652 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}(t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (1+2t){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345652 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345652 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21ddf266-a502-52e7-9722-392dfd92faaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345819 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345819 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345819 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3615743c-9a59-5828-a5f9-76c3c49cabeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345932 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345932 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345932 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "434dca2b-bb1e-5b6a-a0fc-484d397d614c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346102 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346102 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346102 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "581d572d-6189-5f30-8179-ad07a3ead556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346288 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346288 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346288 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c04748c-785f-5be6-8f54-c3dd0b0f7a20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346369 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}(2t-1){e}^{t} \\\\ (1-t){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346369 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346369 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7345187f-4860-54a2-b08f-2475beaa1d97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347460 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347460 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347460 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ef0a53e5-676f-5cb8-9cd4-65e20571d1dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186346102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347765 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5d1be337-4b04-5f96-942e-67689c075869" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186346369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347889 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1a6eed3-c8a4-5660-aaac-2d37375ee8a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348421 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348421 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348421 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348421 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of the system's matrix is $\\lambda =1.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348421 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "608190d5-e5cd-5f82-85c0-726eb6ec9bc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348421 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is $\\lambda =1$ (of multiplicity two). For this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution to the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3-1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -1-1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{w}_{1}+4{w}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{w}_{1}-2{w}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the first equation is a constant multiple of the second. So, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{1}=-1-2{w}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{2}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{2}=0,$  we get ${w}_{1}=-1,$ and therefore\n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}-([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2t-1){e}^{t} \\\\ (1-t){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348782 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348782 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348782 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26f60048-7d7c-5687-9ef2-9d7a40e3cd6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348840 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348840 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348840 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ce3934e-26ad-50c3-b8ad-8eb9aeefecd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348917 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348917 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348917 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34571999-a224-5304-b6f7-661d75ad824f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349840 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349840 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349840 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9c5c0860-4e19-5581-8cad-9596b9de6b84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350167 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350167 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350167 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2004d97-ccfe-5f1f-a183-c402f97fd670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186349840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350799 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "35dc67a9-2544-5970-b757-6ab8a5b07cd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351187 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351187 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351187 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351187 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$\n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of the system's matrix is $\\lambda =5.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351187 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef21bab9-f763-5bd8-b177-dccd5650b9c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351187 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (of multiplicity two). For this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7-5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3-5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{w}_{1}-2{w}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{w}_{1}-2{w}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the first equation is the same as the second. So, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{1}={w}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{2}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=1,b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $a+b=\\frac{3}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
